# WN22-SO-000180: Windows Server 2022 unencrypted passwords must not be sent to third-party Server Message Block (SMB) servers.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000180-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 unencrypted passwords must not be sent to third-party Server Message Block (SMB) servers.`
    description `Some non-Microsoft SMB servers only support unencrypted (plain-text) password authentication. Sending plain-text passwords across the network when authenticating to an SMB server reduces the overall security of the environment. Check with the vendor of the SMB server to determine if there is a way to support encrypted password authentication.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:IA-5(1)(C)`
    control_objective `WN22-SO-000180`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to third-party SMB servers to "Disabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_IA_5_1_C `Windows Server implements IA-5(1)(C) by setting registry value 'EnablePlainTextPassword' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters`
        name `EnablePlainTextPassword`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
